ecosystem_cleanup:
  state: active; public source prepares 1.1.1 dated 2026-09-12 for authorized initial server seeds, cached/default startup and Advanced acquisition controls. Historical publication receipts remain unchanged.
  fixed: Preview server now serves only explicitly declared readable public artifacts; private repository files, source tools, traversal, links, unexpected hosts and unsupported methods are refused.
  consolidation: tools/public-artifact-policy.js is the single path policy for preview, checksum generation and manifest generation; duplicated broad directory-prefix publication rules were removed.
  verification: Seven real-HTTP/policy tests passed; preview line coverage 96.39 percent and policy coverage 100 percent. No new browser installation, source checkout or model copy was created.
  publication_inputs: Metadata builders now read one full policy-bound canonical Git commit and emit only stdout; no copied stage, hardcoded version or output-path override. The publisher reads canonical files, validates the exact manifest and whole public closure, then hashes the read-locked upload stream before any remote write. Prepared source is refused by transport.
  publication_tests: Fourteen tests passed, including 30 actual PowerShell checks with in-memory transport. Route-smoke headings are checked against committed bytes before publication. Historical source, publication and failure receipts remain unchanged.
  stage_retirement: All 27 files under deploy/staging/1.1.0 match the closed historical manifest exactly (87,424 logical bytes). Automatic approval review rejected physical deletion with reason blocked by policy; the stage still exists. tools/remove-reviewed-stage.ps1 provides an exact-hash user-run retirement; no space recovery is claimed.
  stage_review: artifacts/ecosystem-cleanup-20260912/stage-retirement.json; SHA-256 f8cddffc1516e1ec88558b62442f1ae8b95a675ed537f8a0b30ab40ee32f9d22
  prepared_source_verification: All 14 tooling/HTTP tests passed after the documentation changes. Actual Edge checked home and updates at 1440 and 390 pixels; prepared labels were correct, no horizontal overflow or page errors occurred, and diagram text stayed within its SVG bounds. The owned browser profile was removed.
  canonical_byte_lesson: Windows autocrlf expanded public checkout bytes despite LF Git objects. Explicit public-path LF attributes and canonical LF files now keep preview/upload bytes identical to committed digests. The new direct-source publisher refuses drift instead of relying on a copied Git-export stage.
  metadata_workflow: Commit reviewed public content first; write checksum stdout only to canonical docs/file-checksums.sha256 and commit it; then write manifest stdout only to canonical deploy/site-deployment-manifest.v1.json from that checksum-inclusive commit. Validate all canonical public bytes before transport. Never recreate deploy/staging.
  remaining: Complete publication custody review and the wider ecosystem goal; physically retire the policy-blocked stage, establish a qualified starter and prove live server seeding. No new publication or live-model claim.

